The key modeling issue is now isolated: K’s built-in map concatenation is partial on duplicate keys, while the generated obligation requires a total Lean symbol. I’m implementing the canonical `getD`-style completion—use the concrete K map result when defined, otherwise retain the left map—and proving a decomposition lemma that lets every operational rule see a valid K map remainder.
